{"episodes":{"169095":"There were several marine thunderstorm wind gusts in both Galveston Bay and Matagorda Bay.","169210":"A lightning strike caused a house fire.","169263":"A weak front draped across an unstable environment along with enhanced moisture convergence associated with a land breeze and outflow from ongoing thunderstorms led to conditions supportive of waterspouts across an area marked with a non-supercell tornado parameter of 3-4 units.","169351":"The prolonged North American Monsoon pattern prevailed across eastern Utah with abundant moisture present as precipitable water values trended well above normal. Additionally, morning sunshine allowed the atmosphere to rapidly destabilize over the higher terrain. As a result, another round of strong thunderstorms developed across the region. One storm in San Juan County produced a funnel cloud.","169552":"Afternoon sea breeze thunderstorms produce gusty winds over the coastal waters.","169553":"Afternoon sea breeze thunderstorms produce gusty winds over the coastal waters.","169913":"An isolated severe wind gust occurred just west of Livingston.","169920":"Thunderstorms developed ahead of a cold front across north-central Wisconsin during the afternoon hours on Tuesday (6/28).  The strongest storms produced hail up to quarter size as they tracked through the region.","170118":"Severe thunderstorms that produced up to golf ball size hail near Grantsburg, Wisconsin, north of Polk County, weakened as it moved over northern Polk County. However, these storms managed to produce nickel size hail near McKinley.","170201":"Thunderstorms developed along a stationary front. Some of these storms produced large hail and strong wind gusts.","170289":"A trough hot on the heels of an upper ridge resulted in moist southwesterly flow across the region. Approaching trough created a weak surface low in the vicinity, which resulted in better surface moisture being advected in from the east. A front provided a source of lift for thunderstorms on this day.","170311":"A very weak southeast flow pattern was across the area with a ridge axis north of the area across SC/GA. Both Gulf and Atlantic coast sea breezes drifted inland in the afternoon with convergence across the interior in the afternoon and early evening which triggered a few strong storms over a diurnally unstable airmass.","170563":"A high cloud-base shower collapsed and produced a dry microburst near the South Big Horn County Airport in Greybull, WY. The maximum wind gust was 66 mph.","170658":"A severe thunderstorm downed two trees across County Road SD near Watson in Marquette County on the afternoon of the 28th.","170944":"A cold front moved across northwest Wisconsin during the early afternoon hours of the 28th. As this front collided with a warm and moist air mass, storms developed with the strongest storms producing hail across some areas. The largest size was that of a golf ball.","171337":"Scattered storms moved across portions of southeast Minnesota during the late afternoon of June 28th. These storms produced a 60 mph wind gust in Rochester (Olmsted County) that blew down some trees. At least one of the trees landed on a house. Golf ball sized hail fell in Grand Meadow (Mower County).","171434":"A strong thunderstorm moved over Minneapolis Shoal Light on the evening of the 28th.","171517":"An isolated thunderstorm produced a microburst that damaged a barn northwest of Odem.","171518":"A line of thunderstorms developed over the coastal plains of the Middle Texas coast by early evening. The storms moved through the coastal waters by late evening, producing wind gusts from 35 to 40 knots from Seadrift south to Port Aransas.","171530":"A typical summertime pattern prevailed with scattered afternoon thunderstorms across the tri-state region. There were scattered reports of wind damage with the strongest storms.","171643":"A shortwave trough rotated over the northern Great Lakes on 6/28, helping to support a cluster of thunderstorms that initiated across the eastern upper peninsula of Michigan during the afternoon. These storms passed over Paradise, where they produced 0.75 hail stones just before moving over Whitefish Bay.","171644":"A cluster of storms initiated over the eastern Upper Peninsula during the afternoon of 6/28. These storms produced 0.75 hail as they moved over Whitefish Bay.","171841":"An increase of monsoonal moisture resulted in multiple storms with microburst wind gusts in northern Utah, as well as flash flooding in portions of southern Utah."},"events":[{"begin":"2022-06-28T00:09Z","county":"Polk","damageCrops":"0.00K","damageProperty":"0.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2022-06-28T00:09Z","endLat":45.57,"endLon":-92.18,"episode":170118,"id":1031191,"injuries":0,"lat":45.57,"location":"Mckinley","lon":-92.18,"magnitude":0.88,"source":"Trained Spotter","state":"WI","type":"Hail","wfo":"MPX"},{"begin":"2022-06-28T00:16Z","county":"Coastal Waters From Bonita Beach To Englewood Fl Out 20 Nm","damageCrops":"0.00K","damageProperty":"0.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2022-06-28T00:16Z","endLat":26.76,"endLon":-82.06,"episode":169552,"id":1026963,"injuries":0,"lat":26.76,"location":"12.97 E Boca Grande","lon":-82.06,"magnitude":38.0,"magnitudeType":"EG","narrative":"CWOP site GW1989 Punta Gorda reported a 44 mph wind gust.","source":"Mesonet","state":"Gulf Of Mexico","type":"Marine Thunderstorm Wind","wfo":"TBW"},{"begin":"2022-06-28T00:21Z","county":"Tampa Bay","damageCrops":"0.00K","damageProperty":"0.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2022-06-28T00:21Z","endLat":27.97,"endLon":-82.53,"episode":169552,"id":1026962,"injuries":0,"lat":27.97,"location":"8.84 NNE Old Tampa Bay","lon":-82.53,"magnitude":38.0,"magnitudeType":"MG","narrative":"ASOS site KTPA Tampa International Airport reported a 44 mph wind gust.","source":"ASOS","state":"Gulf Of Mexico","type":"Marine Thunderstorm Wind","wfo":"TBW"},{"begin":"2022-06-28T00:30Z","county":"San Antonio, Mesquite, And Espiritu Santo Bays","damageCrops":"0.00K","